{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>After these things and it was told, etc.</b> On his return from Mount Moriah, Abraham was thinking and saying: If my son had been slaughtered, he would already be gone childless — I should have married him to a woman from the daughters of Aner, Eshcol, and Mamre. The Holy One, blessed be He, announced to him that Rebekah, his destined match, had been born. And this is <b>these things</b> — the thoughts of matters that came about through the binding." "<b>She too.</b> She also set her families equal to Abraham's families — twelve: just as from Abraham came twelve tribes that issued from Jacob, eight from the wives and four from the concubines, so too these — eight from wives and four from a concubine."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:59.623202040Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}